<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baton Rouge</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baton Rouge is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> and the capital of the US state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>. A French post in the 18th century, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1763 as part of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1779. In 1810 American settlers seized its Spanish fort and declared the Republic of West Florida, soon annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baton-rouge.jpg" alt="Baton Rouge" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spatms · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Baton_Rouge,_Louisiana_from_Tiger_Stadium_(LSU).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
